# DF CLONE-BEAM discriminator (14z-101) — the maintainer's precise question:
# in Phobos' DF clone-train mode, each clone should fire a beam when he
# attacks (cooldown; damage+hitstun, chip on block). On our build the beam
# SOUND is audible but no beams are seen — graphical-only, or fully missing
# except the sound? Sound fires from the anim node even when a spawn dies,
# so it discriminates nothing; this rig separates the layers:
#   - P2 is parked in the FAR corner and P1 attacks with WHIFFED NORMALS
#     from the far left — his fists cannot reach, so ANY P2 damage/chip is
#     clone-beam contact (the mechanical limb, measured on P2 HP);
#   - pool/effect dumps around each attack answer "do beam OBJECTS spawn";
#   - obj_records_dump at the same frames answers "does anything DRAW".
#
# Pokes (replay-85 doctrine; P2 Victor, stocks banked):
# POKES="1400:ff8782:10;1450:ff8782:10;1500:ff8782:10;1400:ff8b82:03;1450:ff8b82:03;1500:ff8b82:03;3100:ff8509:03;3120:ff8509:03"
300-305 sys=C1
420-425 sys=C2
800-803 sys=S1
940-943 sys=S2
1100-1102 p2=R
1160-1162 p2=R
1300-1302 p1=1
1360-1362 p2=1
# park both: P2 walks to the right corner, P1 to the left corner
2800-3100 p2=R
2800-3100 p1=L
# activate Dark Force: HP+HK with stocks poked at f3100/f3120
3260-3263 p1=36
# brief movement so the clone train materializes (rig-99 measured: the
# mode enters seq 0x18 at ~3323 and movement forms the train)
3340-3420 p1=R
3425-3500 p1=L
# whiffed standing normals from the far corner — clones should answer
# each with a beam; spaced wider than any plausible cooldown
3550-3552 p1=1
3700-3702 p1=1
3850-3852 p1=2
4000-4002 p1=3
4400 wait
